      "language": "en",
      "title": "Forgot something? Koreans say 아 맞다! (Oh, right!) #learnkorean",
      "text": "아 맞다! (a matda) = “Oh, right!” — what Koreans say the moment they suddenly remember something.\r\n\r\n아 맞다, 우산! — Oh right, my umbrella!\r\n…아 맞다! 숙제! — …Oh right! Homework!\r\n\r\nPronunciation: 맞다 sounds like [mat-tta]. The ㅈ closes into a short “t”, and 다 becomes a tense 따.\r\n\r\nWhat do you always forget? Comment: 아 맞다, ____!\r\nSend this to a friend who always forgets 😅\r\n\r\nSYNK LAB · Korean expressions #1 — one everyday expression at a time, with Mongle.\r\n#learnkorean #koreanlanguage #studykorean",
      "alt": [
        "Felt mascot Mongle on a coral cover reading 아 맞다! with the meaning “Oh, right!”"
      ],
